{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.atomic_lp_stability","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.atomic_lp_stability","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.not_atomic_lp_stability_of_junk_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.not_atomic_lp_stability_of_junk_data","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/atomic_lp_stability.lean#L178-L188","doc":"**And it is refutable at freely-chosen data**, which is why it is named\nrather than carried as a `sorry`.\n\nSame carrier, bare volume identically `1`: nothing annihilates it, so the\nfirst conjunct fails.  Together with `atomic_lp_stability_of_junk_data` this\npins the content of the statement without the Hecke machinery — satisfiable\nand refutable, hence constraining nothing about the atom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.atomic_lp_stability_of_junk_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.atomic_lp_stability_of_junk_data","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/atomic_lp_stability.lean#L164-L176","doc":"**The claim is satisfied by data that has nothing to do with hydrogen.**\n\nOne candidate, always normalised, bare volume identically `0` and dressed\nvolume identically `1`.  No `σ₀`, no `H₂(q)`, no Markov trace.\n\nThis is the precise statement of what was wrong with carrying the two\nconclusions as class fields: an instance could choose exactly this, so a\n`[AtomicLPStabilityContext]` binder assumed nothing whatever. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.dressed_is_lp_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.dressed_is_lp_stable","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/atomic_lp_stability.lean#L156-L162","doc":"The 𝓑₃ dressing stabilises the atom — the second half of the\nhypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.bare_is_lp_unstable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.bare_is_lp_unstable","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/atomic_lp_stability.lean#L149-L154","doc":"Bare hydrogen is LP-unstable — the first half of the hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.atomic_lp_stability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.atomic_lp_stability","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/atomic_lp_stability.lean#L130-L147","doc":"**The claim of `prop:atomic-lp-stability`**, as a proposition over\ncaller-supplied data:\n\n* there is a Markov-normalised candidate annihilating the **bare** traced\n  volume (the bare hydrogen atom is LP-unstable), and\n* there is none annihilating the **dressed** volume (the 𝓑₃ dressing\n  stabilises it).\n\n**Named, not asserted.**  See the module docstring for why neither a\nprojection nor a `sorry` is the honest form here. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:atomic-lp-stability","label":"prop:atomic-lp-stability","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/atomic-lp-stability.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.annihilation_ratios_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.annihilation_ratios_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/atomic_lp_stability.lean#L121-L128","doc":"The bare and dressed annihilation ratios are numerically distinct.\n\nThe substrate instance of `bare_ne_dressed_ratio`; sorry-free, and no\nlonger sensitive to which `q₀` pin the literal records. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.bare_ne_dressed_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.bare_ne_dressed_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/atomic_lp_stability.lean#L100-L119","doc":"**The mechanism, pin-independently.**  For *any* `q > 1.1` the dressed\nratio `q⁻¹⁰` differs from the bare ratio `0.537`.\n\n`q > 1.1` gives `q¹⁰ > 1.1¹⁰ > 2.5`, hence `q⁻¹⁰ < 0.4 < 0.537`.  The\nsubstrate anchor never enters, which is the point: the claim does not\ndepend on which `q₀` pin is in force. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.dressedAnnihilationRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.dressedAnnihilationRatio","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/atomic_lp_stability.lean#L96-L98","doc":"Dressed (𝓑₃-twisted) annihilation ratio `q⁻¹⁰` at the substrate\nvalue `q_0 ≈ 1.109978595554181`. Numerically `≈ 0.352`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.bareAnnihilationRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.bareAnnihilationRatio","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/atomic_lp_stability.lean#L92-L94","doc":"Bare-hydrogen annihilation ratio `λ_s / λ_a` (Markov-trace\neigenvalue ratio of `σ₀` in the degree-2 representation). ","signatureChunk":0}]}